{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"auxiliary-dirty-nagapies","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nDiscovered from ADEVX-117. `RealGitHost.commit_and_push` probes the remote for the target branch with `_ls_remote` and reuses that one result to pick the clone ref and to decide whether to run `checkout -b`.\n\nIf another actor creates the branch on the remote between the probe and the clone, `branch_exists` is still false. The clone takes the base ref, the code creates the branch locally from the base, and the final `push origin <branch>` hits a non-fast-forward failure and raises.\n\nThe window is narrow and the trigger is rare, and the prior code had the same single-probe shape, so this is not a regression introduced by ADEVX-117. Moving the probe above the clone widened the window from the length of a clone-and-checkout to the length of a clone.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nTwo concurrent commit activities targeting the same agent branch, or a branch created by an operator while an activity is mid-clone.\n\n## Approach\n\nRe-probe after the clone, or push with a lease and treat the non-fast-forward as a retryable signal to re-resolve the ref. The second is preferable because it closes the window rather than shrinking it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A branch created between the probe and the clone no longer produces a non-fast-forward push failure. Proved by a test that creates the branch on the remote inside a patched `_git` clone call.\n- [ ] The existing idempotency and clone-ref behaviour is unchanged. Proved by `pytest tests/integration/test_github_real_backend.py`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/integration/test_github_real_backend.py` against a bare local remote, with the interleaving forced by patching `_git`.","id":"cdcd-8e4c-5f2c-4c0a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["adevx","follow-on","git-host"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Branch existence is probed before the clone, leaving a TOCTOU window"},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789510394501365001,"uuid":"fdcc5027-4ad8-44b0-8157-719e0a8d0f12"}